{"abstract":"In the field of microservices, Model-Driven Engineering has emerged as a powerful methodology for architectural design, and new programming languages have introduced language abstractions to deal with microservice development more effectively. In this article, we present the first preliminary investigation of how the two approaches can be married, taking the LEMMA framework and the Jolie programming language as respective representatives. By developing a conceptual metamodel for Jolie, we elicit a strong link between the two approaches, which shows that there is much to gain. We discuss a few low-hanging fruits that come from our finding and present some interesting future directions that arise from our new viewpoint.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Giallorenzo, Saverio","Montesi, Fabrizio","Peressotti, Marco","Rademacher, Florian","Sachweh, Sabine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-607186"],"event":{"acronym":"COORDINATION","end":"2021-06-18","place":"Valletta, mt","start":"2021-06-14","title":"16th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Giallorenzo, Saverio"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","UNSA) and INRIA","University of Applied Sciences and Arts Dortmund","University of Bologna"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"jolie and lemma model driven engineering and programming languages meet on microservices","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2104.02458","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-607186","identifier":[{"id":"85111359157","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-76a3be04-443a-4daa-a654-33cd6a2f3de1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C3617F48522BF20F8E3027D7286A9EA8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2104.02458","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"unsa and inria","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"UNSA) and INRIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of applied sciences and arts dortmund","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Applied Sciences and Arts Dortmund","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Saverio","key":"giallorenzopau","last":"Giallorenzo","name":"Giallorenzo, Saverio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"peressottipau","last":"Peressotti","locid":"afca1964-ceda-46fa-b7c7-f6e77e401024","name":"Peressotti, Marco","orcid":"0000-0002-0243-0480","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Florian","key":"rademacherpau","last":"Rademacher","name":"Rademacher, Florian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabine","key":"sachwehpau","last":"Sachweh","name":"Sachweh, Sabine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ferruccio","key":"damianipedh","last":"Damiani","name":"Damiani, Ferruccio","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ornela","key":"dardhapedh","last":"Dardha","name":"Dardha, Ornela","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-78142-2_17","eisbn":["9783030781422"],"isbn":["9783030781415"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"276-284","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"23rd IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference, COORDINATION 2021, Held as Part of the 16th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2021, Valletta, Malta, June 14–18, 2021, Proceedings","title":"Coordination Models and Languages","volume":"12717"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111359157"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-76a3be04-443a-4daa-a654-33cd6a2f3de1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Jolie and LEMMA: Model-Driven Engineering and Programming Languages Meet on Microservices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-607186","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Automated market makers (AMMs) are one of the most prominent decentralized finance (DeFi) applications. They allow users to exchange units of different types of crypto-assets, without the need to find a counter-party. There are several implementations and models for AMMs, featuring a variety of sophisticated economic mechanisms. We present a theory of AMMs. The core of our theory is an abstract operational model of the interactions between users and AMMs, which can be concretised by instantiating the economic mechanisms. We exploit our theory to formally prove a set of fundamental properties of AMMs, characterizing both structural and economic aspects. We do this by abstracting from the actual economic mechanisms used in implementations and identifying sufficient conditions which ensure the relevant properties. Notably, we devise a general solution to the arbitrage problem, the main game-theoretic foundation behind the economic mechanisms of AMMs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bartoletti, Massimo","Chiang, James Hsin yu","Lluch Lafuente, Alberto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-354932"],"event":{"end":"2021-06-18","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2021-06-14","title":"23<sup>rd</sup> IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference on Coordination Models and Languagesec 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chiang, James Hsin yu"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cagliari"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a theory of automated market makers in defi","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/262630410/A_theory_of_Automated_Market_Makers_in_DeFi.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Massimo Bartoletti is partially supported by Conv. Fondazione di Sardegna & Atenei Sardi project F74I19000900007 ADAM. James Hsin-yu Chiang is supported by the PhD School of DTU Compute. Alberto Lluch Lafuente is partially supported by the EU H2020-SU-ICT-03-2018 Project No. 830929 CyberSec4Europe (cybersec4europe.eu). Acknowledgements. Massimo Bartoletti is partially supported by Conv. Fondazione"],"id":"S01-000.00-354932","identifier":[{"id":"85111390267","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a8b43562-56f5-4a05-8fe9-2da4d4d4099d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-353D05E38746DD363134CB86C32115D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/262630410/A_theory_of_Automated_Market_Makers_in_DeFi.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of cagliari","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cagliari","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Formal Methods"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Massimo","key":"bartolettipau","last":"Bartoletti","name":"Bartoletti, Massimo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"James Hsin yu","key":"chiangpau","last":"Chiang","locid":"43ec98ef-0456-414b-88af-bbab62292e2c","name":"Chiang, James Hsin yu","orcid":"0000-0002-5126-9494","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alberto","key":"lluchlafuentepau","last":"Lluch-Lafuente","locid":"8a0c36a1-ada1-4d08-9c86-3c67b5a4a401","name":"Lluch Lafuente, Alberto","name_org":"Lluch-Lafuente, Alberto","orcid":"0000-0001-7405-0818","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ferruccio","key":"damianipedh","last":"Damiani","name":"Damiani, Ferruccio","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ornela","key":"dardhapedh","last":"Dardha","name":"Dardha, Ornela","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-78142-2_11","isbn":["9783030781415"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"168-187","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Coordination Models and Languages"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111390267"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a8b43562-56f5-4a05-8fe9-2da4d4d4099d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A Theory of Automated Market Makers in DeFi","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-354932","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We develop a novel approach for run-time global adaptation of microservice applications, based on synthesis of architecture-level reconfiguration orchestrations. More precisely, we devise an algorithm for automatic reconfiguration that reaches a target system Maximum Computational Load by performing optimal deployment orchestrations. To conceive and simulate our approach, we introduce a novel integrated timed architectural modeling/execution language based on an extension of the actor-based object-oriented Abstract Behavioral Specification (ABS) language. In particular, we realize a timed extension of SmartDeployer, whose ABS code annotations make it possible to express architectural properties. Our Timed SmartDeployer tool fully integrates time features of ABS and architectural annotations by generating timed deployment orchestrations. We evaluate the applicability of our approach on a realistic microservice application taken from the literature: an Email Pipeline Processing System. We prove its effectiveness by simulating such an application and by comparing architecture-level reconfiguration with traditional local scaling techniques (which detect scaling needs and enact replications at the level of single microservices). Our comparison results show that our approach avoids cascading slowdowns and consequent increased message loss and latency, which affect traditional local scaling.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bacchiani, Lorenzo","Bravetti, Mario","Giallorenzo, Saverio","Mauro, Jacopo","Talevi, Iacopo","Zavattaro, Gianluigi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-636173"],"event":{"acronym":"COORDINATION","end":"2021-06-18","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2021-06-14","title":"23rd IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference on Coordination Models and Languages, COORDINATION 2021 held as part of 16th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bacchiani, Lorenzo"],"country":["France","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","French Institute for Research in Computer Science and Automation","University of Bologna"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microservice dynamic architecture level deployment orchestration","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/190902568/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-636173","identifier":[{"id":"85111350018","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-dbda4e9b-b6fe-4703-bf45-3ae78ff4aa39"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6E8D315E47C9B73B5210E9962E9A202E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/190902568/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"french institute for research in computer science and automation","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"French Institute for Research in Computer Science and Automation","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorenzo","key":"bacchianipau","last":"Bacchiani","name":"Bacchiani, Lorenzo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario","key":"bravettipau","last":"Bravetti","name":"Bravetti, Mario","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Saverio","key":"giallorenzopau","last":"Giallorenzo","name":"Giallorenzo, Saverio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacopo","key":"mauropau","last":"Mauro","locid":"ad1ad59c-7294-44a8-98d6-d5329b94baac","name":"Mauro, Jacopo","orcid":"0000-0002-5285-2868","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iacopo","key":"talevipau","last":"Talevi","name":"Talevi, Iacopo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gianluigi","key":"zavattaropau","last":"Zavattaro","name":"Zavattaro, Gianluigi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ferruccio","key":"damianipedh","last":"Damiani","name":"Damiani, Ferruccio","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ornela","key":"dardhapedh","last":"Dardha","name":"Dardha, Ornela","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-78142-2_16","eisbn":["9783030781422"],"isbn":["9783030781415"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"257-275","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"23rd IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference, COORDINATION 2021, Held as Part of the 16th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2021, Valletta, Malta, June 14–18, 2021, Proceedings","title":"Coordination Models and Languages"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111350018"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-dbda4e9b-b6fe-4703-bf45-3ae78ff4aa39"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Microservice Dynamic Architecture-Level Deployment Orchestration","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-636173","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Business processes, data, and run-time control state are all key elements in the design of enterprise applications. However, the different layers for processes, data, and control are usually represented using different technologies that must be explicitly combined and kept in sync. We introduce ReGraDa, a process definition and programming language inspired by the declarative business process language Dynamic Condition Response Graphs and targeting the integrated description of business processes, data and run-time state as reactive graph data. ReGraDa processes compile directly to a data-centric graph-based system (neo4j/cypher), allowing for the database system to manage a process without the need for an external execution engine. The underlying graph structure allows for the definition of native data relations between data elements that subsumes the integrity guaranties of relational and the semi-structured data models. Graph relationships are also used to represent data-dependency and control-flow in the database. We present the reactive semantics of the language, a translation from ReGraDa to cypher, evaluate its performance, and briefly discuss future work and applications.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Galrinho, Leandro","Seco, João Costa","Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Normann, Håkon","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518521"],"event":{"acronym":"COORDINATION","end":"2021-06-18","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2021-06-14","title":"23rd IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference on Coordination Models and Languages, COORDINATION 2021 held as part of 16th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NOVA Laboratory for Computer Science and Informatics","NOVA University Lisbon"],"le