{"abstract":"A session-based process satisfies the progress property if its sessions never get stuck when it is executed in an adequate context. Previous work studied how to define progress by introducing the notion of catalysers, execution contexts generated from the type of a process. In this paper, we refine such definition to capture a more intuitive notion of context adequacy for checking progress. Interestingly, our new catalysers lead to a novel characterisation of progress in terms of the standard notion of lock-freedom. Guided by this discovery, we also develop a conservative extension of catalysers that does not depend on types, generalising the notion of progress to untyped session-based processes. We combine our results with existing techniques for lock-freedom, obtaining a new methodology for proving progress. Our methodology captures new processes wrt previous progress analysis based on session types.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Dardha, Ornela","Montesi, Fabrizio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381303"],"event":{"acronym":"COORDINATION","title":"International Conference on Coordination Models and Languages"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Catalysers","Context adequacy","Lock freedom","Progress property","Session based processes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"progress as compositional lock freedom","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-43376-8_4","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381303","identifier":[{"id":"84902583426","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0329c3b7-3920-4332-9d07-06ee80b16596"],"keyword":["Catalysers","Context adequacy","Lock-freedom","Progress property","Session-based processes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-95DCD6845E752D2CB734DDAC8BF89FC9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-43376-8_4","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ornela","key":"dardhapau","last":"Dardha","locid":"b6c98930-e1c7-422f-bb9c-808f1394344a","name":"Dardha, Ornela","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-43376-8_4","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"49-64","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902583426"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0329c3b7-3920-4332-9d07-06ee80b16596"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"